Z||000000||Hybrid2M6||11-20-2001||01:43 PM||||I was just wondering if this would be possible to do. What I had in mind was to cut the lower section off and mold it back on a little bit lower. Then smooth all of the lines that seperate the black area to the red area and paint to match. What do you think?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newrearmod_2.jpg"> <BR>(I know this isn't my car, so I apologise to who ever's fiero I hacked to death.)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChopTop||11-20-2001||02:11 PM||||While I'm no fan of the tacked on side pieces, I do like the molded in ground effects of the front and rear facias. <BR>From your rendering it initially appears a little slab sided.  But sometimes pics don't do ideas justice, it might look really good in person. ||||reg||1
